---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="AIF">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <header class="mb-12 text-center" transition:animate="fade">
            <img
                src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hydle-Research-Group/media/refs/heads/main/logos/aif.svg"
                width="25%"
            />
            <h1 class="text-5xl mb-4">
                A certification for projects that void the use of AI
            </h1>
        </header>

        <div
            class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none"
            transition:animate="fade"
        >
            Certified-AIF (AIF for short) is a no-cost logo that can be applied
            to any project that wasn't made by AI or Generative AI such as LLMs <i
                >(with exceptions.)</i
            >

            <h3>Definitions</h3>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    By "AI", "Generative AI", "AI-generated", or
                    Artificial-Intelligence, we define it as "any text, images,
                    audio, or video generated entirely by digital systems and/or
                    neural networks." This includes the prompting device written
                    by humans, regardless if the human interfered or not during
                    the generative process.
                </li>
                <li>
                    By "element of creation", we define it as "anything that is
                    created or made."
                </li>
                <li>
                    By "real people", we define it as "any individual human
                    being with consciousness."
                </li>
                <li>
                    By "asset(s)", we define it as "any binary data and/or
                    individual files that an element of creation may rely upon
                    to function."
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Requirements</h3>

            In order to certify a project, organization, or any element of
            creation with the AIF, the following requirements must be met:
            <br /><br />
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>No.1</b>
                    The element of creation made no use of AI during its construction
                    and/or conceptualization.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>No.2</b>
                    The element of creation isn't actively using AI during new logic
                    implementations and/or updates.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>No.3</b>
                    The element of creation doesn't use AI on any subsidiaries and/or
                    additional elements of creation.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>No.4</b>
                    The element of creation doesn't contain AI-generated assets, such
                    as images, audio, video.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Exceptions</h3>

            The AIF allows strict exceptions in which the use of AI doesn't
            violate it:
            <br /><br />
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>No.1</b>
                    The element of creation includes language translations created
                    by AI. If the text was originally constructed by real humans (Requirements
                    No.1), then translated to another language using AI, the AIF can
                    still be applied to the element of creation.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>No.2</b>
                    The element of creation includes the implementation of AI. If
                    still constructed by real humans (Requirements No.1), and maintained
                    by real humans (Requirements No.2), then the implementation of
                    an AI is allowed to use the AIF.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>How To Use</h3>

            To apply the AIF to an element of creation, you can download the SVG
            logo <a
                href="https://github.com/Hydle-Research-Group/media/blob/main/logos/aif.svg"
                >here</a
            >. The logo can be used anywhere in an element of creation, <b
                >as long as</b
            > all requirements described above are met.
            <br /><br />
            <i
                >Modifying the logo is not allowed and heavily discouraged. Any
                modification will result in an invalid AIF element of creation.</i
            >
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
